        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1314171698,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "Some of the indigenous peoples of the region consume the plant as a food source. The immature flowering stalks are sweet and juicy and easy to harvest. People either eat them raw or brew them into alcoholic beverages. The leaf bases are also edible, but require roasting to destroy unpleasant chemical compounds",
